    "last_model_intent_unverified": "The fix is complete and minimal.\n\n**Root cause:** `OrderedMultiDict` inherits from `dict`, so `copy.copy`/`copy.deepcopy` used the default `dict.__reduce_ex__(4)`, which returns a 5-tuple whose 5th element is a `list_iterator` of pairs. `copy._reconstruct` then replays those pairs via `y[key] = value`, which deduplicates repeated keys and keeps only the last value.\n\n**Fix:** Added `__reduce__` returning the 3-tuple `(type(self), (), self.__getstate__())`. This routes copying through the existing `__getstate__`/`__setstate__` pair, which preserves every pair and its order via `update_extend`, while `copy` still handles memoization for shared/self references and deep-copying of values. `type(self)` preserves the concrete subclass, and pickle behavior is unchan…",
